Revision history for Term-ReadLine-GnuWin32

1.470_001  2026-10-21
    - Initial Windows-only developer release, based on Term::ReadLine::Gnu
      1.47 and bundled GNU Readline 8.3.
    - Require Windows 11, Perl 5.44, and Visual C++ 2026; target x64/ARM64.
    - Distribute through GitHub as Term-ReadLine-GnuWin32, providing the
      compatible Term::ReadLine::Gnu package for automatic discovery and
      CPAN GNU command completion; do not upload this fork to PAUSE.
    - Build with standard MakeMaker targets and native Perl build helpers.
    - Keep XS sources, typemaps, portability headers, and generated C/object
      files together in xs/; omit generated files from source releases.
    - Preserve pristine Readline sources and apply verified local patches.
    - Include console, Unicode, callback, debugger, and REPL regression tests.
    - Check 64-bit sizes and Perl integers at Readline's int API boundaries;
      preserve multibyte error sentinels and use 64-bit file offsets.
    - Add GPLv3-or-later project licensing and upstream component notices.

The original module history is retained in docs/UPSTREAM_CHANGES.
Developer version 1.470_001 sorts above upstream 1.47; the next stable fork release
must advance to at least 1.471.
